  "description": "<div>\n<p>Look for <code>word</code> in a rectangular grid of letters. A match starts on any cell and proceeds to horizontally or vertically adjacent cells; a cell cannot be used twice in one path. Return whether such a path exists.</p>\n<p>Diagonal moves do not count. If the board is empty, return <code>false</code>. The word is always nonempty, and character comparisons are case-sensitive.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> board = [[&quot;A&quot;,&quot;B&quot;,&quot;C&quot;,&quot;E&quot;],[&quot;S&quot;,&quot;F&quot;,&quot;C&quot;,&quot;S&quot;],[&quot;A&quot;,&quot;D&quot;,&quot;E&quot;,&quot;E&quot;]], word = &quot;ABCCED&quot;\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The path bends through adjacent cells without reusing one.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> board = [[&quot;A&quot;,&quot;B&quot;],[&quot;C&quot;,&quot;D&quot;]], word = &quot;ABCD&quot;\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The desired continuation would require a diagonal step or revisiting a cell.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> board = [], word = &quot;A&quot;\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> There are no cells on an empty board.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>0 &lt;= board.length &lt;= 6</code></li>\n<li>If there are rows, <code>1 &lt;= board[i].length &lt;= 6</code> and all rows have equal length</li>\n<li><code>1 &lt;= word.length &lt;= 15</code></li>\n<li>Board cells and word contain uppercase English letters</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
